BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:16th Australasian Workshop on Econometrics and Health Economics
DTSTART:20270331T120000
DTEND:20270402T130000
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will provide a forum for the development and dis
 semination of applications of econometrics and other quantitative approach
 es in health economics. It will follow the format of the long-running Euro
 pean workshops on econometrics and health economics.\n\nWe are now calling
  for papers for presentation\, with up to 14 papers to be accepted. Presen
 tations by doctoral students and early career researchers are encouraged.
 \n\nPapers accepted for presentation will each be allocated 50 minutes\, i
 ncluding 30 minutes for the author’s presentation\, 10 minutes for an ap
 pointed discussant and 10 minutes for general discussion.\n\nThe number of
  workshop participants is strictly limited and participants will be expect
 ed to attend the full workshop. <br/>Please see the drop-down below for mo
 re information on papers\, including the submission deadline.\n\nKeynote S
 peakers\n\n<!-- false -->\n<div class="accordion nested-accordion js-front
 end-complex-accordion" id="Component-4429809" role="tablist">\n<div class=
 "hidden">\n<span class="hidden nested-accordion__expand-text">View</span>
 \n<span class="hidden nested-accordion__collapse_text">Close</span>\n</div
 >\n<section class="panel section1 Paper_submissions-1 close">\n<h3 aria-co
 ntrols="Paper_submissions-1" aria-expanded="false" class="accTitle" data-c
 lick-event="monash.accordion.toggle" data-expanded-by-default="false" data
 -position="1" data-title="Paper submissions" data-type="nested" id="Paper_
 submissions-1" role="tab">\n<span class="accTitle__icon"><svg><use href="h
 ttps://www.monash.edu/__data/assets/git_bridge/0009/2651868/dist/assets/im
 ages/icon-spritesheet.svg?h=00fceca7#copy"></use></svg></span>\n<span clas
 s="accTitle__text">Paper submissions</span>\n<span class="accTitle__toggle
 -wrapper">\n<a class="accTitle__toggle" href="#Paper_submissions-1" rel="1
 ">\n<span class="accTitle__toggle-text">View</span>\n<span class="accTitle
 __toggle-arrow"><img alt="View" src="https://www.monash.edu/__data/assets/
 file/0011/2179901/arrow-outline-right.svg"/></span>\n</a>\n</span>\n</h3>
 \n<div aria-labelledby="Paper_submissions-1" class="accContent" role="tabp
 anel" style="display: none\;">\n<div class="accContent__inner">\n<div clas
 s="accContent__wrapper">\n<div id="component_4429813">\n<p>Please submit a
  full draft of the paper OR a 1000-word (minimum) abstract by <strong>18 D
 ecember 2026</strong>.</p><h3>Abstract criteria</h3><p>If sending an abstr
 act\, it should be structured to include <strong>details of the aims</stro
 ng>\, the <strong>econometric methods used</strong> (in the past some abst
 racts have not contained econometric detail so we have been unable to prop
 erly assess them)\, and <strong>results</strong>.</p><p>Results should be 
 included even if they are preliminary. Abstracts containing no results or 
 no details of the econometric methods will be less likely to be accepted.<
 /p><p>Abstracts and papers will be judged primarily on the quality of thei
 r econometrics content. We strongly encourage presentation and discussion 
 of work in progress. Papers already submitted to or accepted by journals a
 re discouraged.</p><h3>Fees for invited participants</h3><div>Those invite
 d to participate will be asked to pay the registration fee in February 202
 7.</div><ul><li>Full registration: AU$650</li><li>PhD students: AU$250</li
 ><li>Low and middle income countries: AU$300*</li></ul><p>*A citizen resid
 ing in a country on the <a href="https://datahelpdesk.worldbank.org/knowle
 dgebase/articles/906519-world-bank-country-and-lending-groups">World Bank 
 list</a> of low and middle income countries.</p><h4>Inclusions</h4><ul><li
  aria-level="1" style="list-style-type:disc">Two nights' accommodation at 
 Q Station on Wednesday 31st and Thursday 1st of April.</li><li aria-level=
 "1" style="list-style-type:disc">All meals from lunch on Wednesday 31st to
  lunch on Friday 2nd of April.</li></ul><p>For additional nights\, you wil
 l need to organise them with the hotel directly.</p><h3>Submissions and re
 gistering your interest to attend</h3><p>Electronic submission of papers i
 s required and can be uploaded using the link below. When submitting\, you
  will be able to choose whether you would like to present a paper\, discus
 s a paper or chair a session.</p><p><a class="btn" href="https://monash.sy
 d1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_4Myq5yKm0nwOjIy" target="_blank">Submit your 
 paper</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n<script
